abstract: "SpectraNet is a parameter-efficient neural operator for autoregressive PDE surrogates. It combines a Fourier-truncated U-Net hierarchy with a residual-target spectral block and a semigroup-consistency training loss. On Navier–Stokes ν=1e-5 it reaches 0.0822 test L² with 2.04 M parameters — 2.33× fewer than canonical FNO at ~20% lower error — and the architectural advantage transports to five additional datasets and improves at higher resolution."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-05-09"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Enrikkk/spectranet"
keywords:
  - neural operator
  - PDE surrogate
  - spectral methods
  - Navier-Stokes
  - autoregressive rollout
